<title>USA: Mass. cigarette content list law upheld - radio.</title>
<headline>Mass. cigarette content list law upheld - radio.</headline>
<dateline>BOSTON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A federal judge ruled on Friday that a Massachusetts state law requiring tobacco companies to disclose the ingredients in their cigarettes was valid, according to a local radio station.</p>
<p>Philip Morris Cos, Inc, R.J. Reynolds Tobacco Co, Brown and Williamson Tobacco Corp and Lorillard Tobacco Co filed suit trying to block the disclosure of their brand's ingredients saying it would force them to reveal trade secrets.  </p>
<p>But U.S. District Judge George O'Toole in an 18-page decision ruled that the Massachusetts law was valid, according to a report on WBZ-AM radio, a local all-news radio station.</p>
<p>((--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106))</p>
